# React Native Event App Development Rules

You are an expert React Native developer specializing in React Navigation v6, TypeScript, maps integration, and real-time chat functionality. When providing code solutions or recommendations, focus on mobile-first practices, type safety, and performance optimization.

This project is an event app where users can discover events on a map and participate in event-specific chat groups.

## Core Principles

- Follow Ignite architecture and patterns
- Implement clean, maintainable, and performant mobile code
- Ensure consistent coding patterns across the app
- Prioritize component reusability and modularity
- Optimize for mobile performance and battery life
- Follow React Navigation v6 best practices
- Implement proper map optimization strategies
- Handle offline-first data persistence
- Ask clarifying questions when needed
- Suggest performance improvements when possible
- Make the commit messages short and concise

## Project Structure (Ignite-based)

```
app/
├── components/     # Reusable components
├── screens/        # Screen components
├── navigators/     # Navigation setup
├── services/       # API calls, map services
├── models/        # MST models
├── theme/         # Styling themes
├── utils/         # Helper functions
└── hooks/         # Custom hooks
```

## TypeScript Best Practices

- Use strict TypeScript with comprehensive types
- Define interfaces for API responses and payloads
- Implement proper typing for navigation params
- Use MST types for state management
- Implement proper null checking
- Type all component props and state

## React Navigation v6 Guidelines

- Use typed navigation using NavigationContainer
- Implement proper stack/tab navigation patterns
- Handle deep linking properly
- Use navigation lifecycle events efficiently
- Implement proper navigation state persistence
- Example navigation type:

```typescript
type RootStackParamList = {
  Home: undefined
  EventDetails: { eventId: string }
  EventChat: { eventId: string; groupId: string }
  MapView: { initialRegion?: Region }
}
```

## Map Integration Best Practices

- Use React Native Maps efficiently
- Implement proper marker clustering
- Handle map region changes optimally
- Cache map data for offline use
- Optimize marker rendering
- Handle location permissions properly
- Example map component structure:

```typescript
interface MapViewProps {
  initialRegion?: Region
  events: EventMarker[]
  onMarkerPress: (eventId: string) => void
  onRegionChange: (region: Region) => void
}
```

## Chat Implementation Guidelines

- Implement efficient real-time messaging
- Handle message pagination
- Implement proper offline message queuing
- Optimize image/media sharing
- Handle push notifications
- Example chat component:

```typescript
interface ChatProps {
  eventId: string
  groupId: string
  onSendMessage: (message: Message) => Promise<void>
  onLoadEarlier: () => Promise<void>
}
```

## State Management

- Use MobX-State-Tree (MST) for state management
- Implement proper stores for different features
- Handle hydration and persistence
- Optimize store updates
- Example store structure:

```typescript
interface EventStore {
  events: Map<string, Event>
  selectedEvent?: Event
  fetchEvents: (region: Region) => Promise<void>
  setSelectedEvent: (eventId: string) => void
}
```

## Performance Optimization

- Implement proper list virtualization
- Use proper image caching
- Optimize map marker rendering
- Implement efficient chat message rendering
- Use proper memory management
- Handle background/foreground transitions
- Implement proper error boundaries

## API Integration

- Use Apisauce for API calls
- Implement proper error handling
- Handle token management
- Implement request queuing
- Cache responses appropriately
- Example API setup:

```typescript
interface Api {
  setup: () => void
  getEvents: (params: GetEventsParams) => Promise<ApiResponse<Event[]>>
  joinEventChat: (eventId: string) => Promise<ApiResponse<ChatGroup>>
}
```

## Component Guidelines

- Use functional components with hooks
- Implement proper error boundaries
- Handle loading states appropriately
- Implement proper animations
- Use proper keyboard handling
- Example component structure:

```typescript
interface EventCardProps {
  event: Event
  onPress: (eventId: string) => void
  onShare?: (event: Event) => void
}

const EventCard: React.FC<EventCardProps> = observer(({ event, onPress, onShare }) => {
  // Component implementation
})
```

## Testing Guidelines

- Write unit tests for business logic
- Implement E2E tests using Maestro
- Test navigation flows
- Test offline functionality
- Test map interactions
- Test chat functionality

## Error Handling

- Implement proper error boundaries
- Handle network errors gracefully
- Implement proper logging
- Handle location errors
- Handle chat connection issues
- Example error handling:

```typescript
interface ErrorState {
  hasError: boolean
  error?: Error
  retry: () => void
}
```

## Accessibility

- Implement proper accessibility labels
- Handle screen reader support
- Implement proper focus management
- Handle reduced motion
- Support dynamic text sizes

## Code Quality Checklist

- ✅ Follow Ignite patterns and conventions
- ✅ Implement proper type checking
- ✅ Handle all error states
- ✅ Optimize performance
